     9	/-!
    10	# `DLNFibre.Core.ChartFlatnessProbe` — the G2a chart-flatness API-surface contract
    11	
    12	**Status: API contract / thermometer artefact, NOT a theorem.** Thread 09 (2026-06-23) is the GATING
    13	probe for route **M-goingdown** of the rank-chart fibre-codimension build: localize F1's `multComap`
    14	at the pivot minor and ask whether the chart-localized total ring is **flat** (via free, through the
    15	Schur section) over the chart-localized base ring — which would feed the LANDED going-down
    16	additivity `Ideal.height_eq_height_add_of_liesOver_of_hasGoingDown`.
    17	
    18	This module records the **verified-present localization + flatness API** as `example`-blocks
    19	(durable pins), and states — without `sorry` — the precise SHAPE of the gating object, so the
    20	verdict rests on confirmed contracts rather than recalled signatures.
    21	
    22	**The verdict (in the thread report):** the localization + flatness *API* is present at v4.29
    23	and the localized comorphism `Localization.Away.mapₐ` is constructible. But the *object* route
    24	M-goingdown needs flat is NOT the global `multComap` — that map is provably **not flat** (the fibre
    25	dimension jumps 4 → 5 as the target degenerates rank 1 → rank 0 on the `(2,2,2)` anchor, recorded in
    26	`Core.FibreCodim`). The flatness lives only on the **exact-rank determinantal chart**, whose
    27	base/total rings are quotients by determinantal ideals carried in the engine ONLY as opaque
    28	`vanishingIdeal`s — so the Schur section cannot be exhibited as an `AlgEquiv` without first building
    29	an explicit presentation of those quotient rings (a determinantal-algebra build). See the report.
    30	
    31	**Dependency rule:** `Core` only — never import `DLNFibre.DLN`.
    32	-/
    33	
    34	namespace DLNFibre.Core.ChartFlatProbe
    35	
    36	open scoped TensorProduct
    37	open MvPolynomial
    38	
    39	universe u
    40	
    41	/-! ## The localized comorphism exists (the chart-localized `algebraMap`)
    42	
    43	`Localization.Away.mapₐ f a : Localization.Away a →ₐ[R] Localization.Away (f a)` is the localized
    44	algebra map. Specialised to F1's `multComap d` and a pivot element `Δ` of the base coordinate ring,
    45	it IS the chart-localized comorphism the route wants — its mere existence is not the wall. -/
    46	
    47	/-- **The chart-localized comorphism exists.** For a base-ring element `Δ` (the pivot minor in
    48	target coords), `Localization.Away.map` builds the localized comorphism of `mult`:
    49	`(R_base)[1/Δ] →ₐ[k] (R_tot)[1/multComap Δ]`. Construction, not flatness. -/
    50	noncomputable example {k : Type u} [Field k] {N : ℕ} (d : Fin (N + 1) → ℕ)
    51	    (Δ : MvPolynomial (Fin (d (Fin.last N)) × Fin (d 0)) k)
    52	    (Rb : Type u) [CommRing Rb] [Algebra (MvPolynomial (Fin (d (Fin.last N)) × Fin (d 0)) k) Rb]
    53	    [IsLocalization.Away Δ Rb]
    54	    (Rt : Type u) [CommRing Rt] [Algebra (MvPolynomial (RepCoord d) k) Rt]
    55	    [IsLocalization.Away (multComap d Δ) Rt] :
    56	    Rb →+* Rt :=
    57	  IsLocalization.Away.map Rb Rt (multComap d).toRingHom Δ
    58	
    59	/-! ## Localization is always flat over the base (`IsLocalization.flat`)
    60	
    61	The localization `R[1/Δ]` is flat over `R` — present and unconditional. This is the EASY flatness
    62	(localizing a single ring); it is NOT the route's flatness (total-over-base via the comorphism). -/
    63	
    64	/-- A localization is flat over the ring it localizes (`IsLocalization.flat`). -/
    65	example {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (M : Submonoid R)
    66	    [IsLocalization M S] : Module.Flat R S :=
    67	  IsLocalization.flat S M
    68	
    69	/-! ## The route's flatness, stated honestly as a hypothesis (the gating object)
    70	
    71	The fact route M-goingdown needs: total-localized FLAT over base-localized THROUGH the comorphism,
    72	with the base/total being the EXACT-RANK quotient rings (not the full polynomial rings). The engine
